WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.300
Just wait, Honda!

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:22.860
We'll get your body back soon!

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:27.700
The Big Five keep switching their Deck Masters.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:31.560
But Yugi and I form an invinicible tag team!

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:38.060
They're about to lose, so why are they laughing?

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:45.020
Defeat Five-Headed Dragon

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:53.330
I was waiting for this moment.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.650
Altar of Mist can activate during this third turn.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.200
What?

00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:01.230
We win this duel!

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.300
Altar of Mist's effect activates!

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:08.240
I add Dragon Revival Ritual from my deck to my hand.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:15.180
Dragon Revival Ritual is a Ritual Spell to summon Five-Headed Dragon.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.450
What?

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:27.390
But I need to tribute Earth, Water, Fire, Wind and Dark Attribute monsters within five turns.

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.820
You won't get monsters with five different Attributes that easily!

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.960
You haven't noticed yet?

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.960
Look behind me.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:41.460
Behind you?

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.240
Jinzo!

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:45.260
I see!

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.680
The Deck Masters!

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:50.080
Judge Man is Earth Attribute.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:52.280
Deepsea Warrior is Water Attribute.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.440
Robotic Knight is Fire Attribute.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.290
Nightmare Penguin is Wind Attribute.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.460
So Jinzo is Dark Attribute?

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.270
Exactly!  Here I go!

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.000
I summon my Deck Master!

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.770
Jinzo!

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:11.500
I summon my Deck Master!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:13.550
Deepsea Warrior!

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:15.550
I summon my Deck Master!

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:17.720
Nightmare Penguin!

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.510
I summon my Deck Master!

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:21.080
Judge Man!

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.080
I summon my Deck Master!

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.770
Robotic Knight!

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.420
I activate Dragon Revival Ritual!

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:37.220
I fuse the Earth, Water, Fire, Wind and Dark Attribute Deck Masters to summon Five-Headed Dragon!

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.090
Five-Headed Dragon!

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.650
Damn!  That thing hurt me last time.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:03.520
I leave the rest to you.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:04.420
Jonouchi!

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.830
Jonouchi...

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:11.120
Jonouchi!

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:14.120
It's going to defeat me again?

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.250
This monster cannot attack during the turn it was summoned.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.910
C'mon.  Don't scare me like that.

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:29.110
But when it's summoned, it destroys all your monsters, spells and traps.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.600
That's dirty!  You tried to mislead me!

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.040
Sorry.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.500
I'll tell you this.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:54.940
Earth, Water, Fire, Wind and Dark Attribute monsters can't damage Five-Headed Dragon.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:59.740
That means most monster attacks won't work!

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:04.420
Five-Headed Dragon combines our strengths.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.220
It is invincible.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:13.700
But we've lost before, so we must be extra careful.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:16.000
I set a card.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.300
I end my turn.

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:22.130
What's wrong, Jonouchi?  It's your turn.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.600
Are you kidding me?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.710
How can we destroy a monster with 5000 attack points?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:31.150
Well, Yugi?

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.380
Fight hard, Jonouchi!

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:34.680
We will get a chance!

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:36.960
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:39.200
I gotta shape up.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:41.310
I can't just rely on Yugi.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.620
My turn!

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:43.420
I draw!

00:05:45.420 --> 00:05:47.750
I have no monsters to summon.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:52.030
But I'll do whatever I can to the end!

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:54.800
I set three cards!

00:05:56.930 --> 00:05:59.900
I'm counting on you, Deck Master!

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.900
I summon my Deck Master, Flame Swordsman!

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:09.960
Jonouchi!  If they destroy your Deck Master, you lose!

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:13.330
If you lose, you'll face the same fate as me!

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:14.400
Brother...

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:18.330
I did everything I could do.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:23.090
In the end, I guess I need to rely on him.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:27.700
I leave the rest to Yugi.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.570
I end my turn!

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.850
Leave it to me, Jonouchi.

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:34.250
We still have a chance.

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.510
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:42.920
I summon my Deck Master, Dark Magician!

00:06:45.310 --> 00:06:49.640
Yugi summoned his Deck Master, just like Jonouchi!

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:51.620
What are they thinking?

00:06:51.620 --> 00:06:59.560
If they have no monsters to summon, a direct attack will defeat them anyway.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:04.330
There's no way to defeat Five-Headed Dragon.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:08.280
Just admit defeat and surrender.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.390
Yugi.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:19.180
If you keep bragging, you'll setting yourself up for humiliation.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.480
What?

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:26.560
You're not the only one who can fuse Deck Masters together!

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:28.080
What?

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.990
Fuse?

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:33.230
Will they become Dragon Master Knight again?

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:45.640
No.  They can't become Dragon Master Knight without Blue-Eyes.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:51.540
I fuse our Deck Masters!  Flame Swordsman and Dark Magician!

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:55.280
I Fusion Summon Dark Flare Knight!

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.240
Dark Flare Knight?

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:20.910
He's allowed to attack the same turn that he's Fusion Summoned.

00:08:22.660 --> 00:08:24.460
Go ahead and try.

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:26.460
That monster is Dark Attribute.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.350
He can't hurt Five-Headed Dragon.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:34.110
Besides, our monster has 5000 attack points.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:38.360
You're going to attack with a monster that has 2200 attack points?

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.820
That's right.

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.230
What?

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:44.620
That means he'll be destroyed!

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:46.110
It's suicide!

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.330
No.  This is Yugi we're talking about.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:50.270
He must have an idea.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:55.970
I don't know what he's thinking, but I trust Yugi.

00:08:55.970 --> 00:09:01.990
Dark Flare Knight attacks Five-Headed Dragon!

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:09.200
You lost your mind, Yugi.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.670
Why didn't you lose life points?

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:33.280
Even if your monster's attack points are greater, I take no damage.

00:09:33.620 --> 00:09:38.320
That's Dark Flare Knight's effect!

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.250
What?

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:41.020
And there's more.

00:09:41.020 --> 00:09:48.680
When this card is destroyed, I can Special Summon Mirage Knight from my deck!

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:58.180
Who cares.

00:09:58.180 --> 00:10:03.830
His attack points are no match for Five-Headed Dragon-

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:08.250
That means he must also have an effect!

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:13.560
Mirage Knight, attack Five-Headed Dragon!

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:25.340
Mirage Knight can't be destroyed in battle.

00:10:27.060 --> 00:10:32.800
And Mirage Knight gains attack points equal to the damage he took.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:40.960
Five-Headed Dragon's 5000 attack points are added to Mirage Knight's attack points!

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:46.620
No way!  7800 attack points?

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:49.620
And I'll tell you one final thing.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:53.080
Mirage Knight is Light Attribute!

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:58.040
This warrior of light is the only one that can attack Five-Headed Dragon!

00:10:58.760 --> 00:11:00.420
From dark to light.

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:02.850
I was waiting for this moment!

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:13.570
Five-Headed Dragon is destroyed!

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:19.620
You lose 2800 life points, so you have 0 life points!

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.620
We win this duel!

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:25.900
What?

00:11:25.900 --> 00:11:28.200
Why don't you have 0 life points?

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.940
What's going on?

00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.630
You must've cheated again!

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:42.620
It seems I'm one step ahead of you.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:45.310
Look at my field.

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:45.980
What?

00:11:47.080 --> 00:11:49.050
A Deal with Dark Ruler?

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:50.080
Yes.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:55.470
When a Level 8-or-higher monster is destroyed, this trap card activates.

00:11:55.470 --> 00:12:03.030
By paying half my life points, this trap negates the damage that my destroyed monster took.

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:06.470
That's why your life points didn't drop to 0.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.060
Not only that.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:14.840
When this trap activates, it summons Berserk Dragon.

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.070
Huh?  Mirage Knight changed back.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:50.140
When the Battle Phase ends, Mirage Knight vanishes.

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:54.250
And Dark Magician and Flame Swordsman are Special Summoned.

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:55.520
This is bad!

00:12:55.520 --> 00:13:02.570
On their next turn, The Big Five will destroy either Yugi or Jonouchi's Deck Master!

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:04.760
So one will lose?

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.740
That can't happen!

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:09.420
Please, Jonouchi!  Try harder!

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:14.040
Even if I want to, it's Yugi's turn.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.380
I'm counting on you, Yugi!

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:20.200
I activate the spell card, Magical Hats!

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:27.480
And my Deck Master's ability, Separate Magic!

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:34.520
By paying 1000 life points, I can use Magical Hats again this turn!

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.850
I end my turn!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:42.880
Nice, Yugi!

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.910
We can now survive!

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:47.940
But only for a while.

00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:49.910
We can't feel safe.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:51.600
It'll be fine.

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.070
He won't pick the right Hat.

00:13:54.420 --> 00:13:57.510
I know you want to believe that.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:03.000
But the truth will crush any hope you have.

00:14:03.020 --> 00:14:05.520
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:17.860
Berserk Dragon's effect allows it to attack four monsters simultaneously.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:20.860
With one attack...

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.300
Four monsters...

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:28.800
Yugi's Dark Magician is in one of his four Magical Hats.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.720
And Flame Swordsman is in Jonouchi's Magical Hats.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:40.750
If he focuses all his attacks on either Yugi or Jonouchi, the odds of picking the right Magical Hat is...

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:41.860
100%!

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:43.290
That means...

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:47.730
Either you or I will lose this turn.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:50.180
Don't be so sure!

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:52.730
Say what?  You dummy!

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:55.340
He's bad at math.

00:14:57.900 --> 00:15:00.830
Then I'll teach you defeat.

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:05.060
By watching your friend lose!

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:12.100
Berserk Dragon attacks Yugi Muto's four Magical Hats!

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:20.630
Is this it?

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:22.560
Don't give up, Yugi!

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.000
Flame Swordsman!

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:27.100
Protect Dark Magician and Yugi!

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:28.530
Jonouchi!

00:15:29.710 --> 00:15:31.140
That's crazy, Jonouchi!

00:15:31.420 --> 00:15:34.070
Jonouchi is going to lose!

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:35.510
Stop, brother!

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:37.680
We don't need more monkeys!

00:15:51.240 --> 00:15:52.660
Jonouchi!

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:59.240
- Jonouchi!
- Brother!

00:15:59.240 --> 00:15:59.930
Why?

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:00.940
Impossible!

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:12.100
Why is Flame Swordsman alive?

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:15.120
This saved me.

00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.480
Silver Dollar?

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:19.600
Yeah!

00:16:19.600 --> 00:16:25.020
When a monster with 1000-or-fewer attack points is about to be destroyed...

00:16:25.020 --> 00:16:28.330
...this trap card negates that damage!

00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:31.860
1000-or-fewer attack points...  I see!

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:35.400
Flame Swordsman has 1800 attack points.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:41.460
But by using his Deck Master's ability, he has less than 1000 attack points.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.800
That's why the trap activated.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:48.430
You thought that far.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:50.630
Impressive, Jonouchi!

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.050
Now we're square.

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.590
What'll you do now, The Big Five?

00:16:55.590 --> 00:17:00.020
Damn!  You're so lucky!

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.530
I end my turn!

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:05.900
Its attack points decreased?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:13.210
When my turn ends, Berserk Dragon loses 500 attack points.

00:17:13.370 --> 00:17:16.560
I see!  That's too bad!

00:17:16.560 --> 00:17:17.980
My turn!

00:17:17.980 --> 00:17:19.010
I draw!

00:17:20.780 --> 00:17:22.930
I flip over my spell card!

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.600
I activate Knight's Title!

00:17:26.290 --> 00:17:29.970
Yugi's Dark Magician changes to Warrior-Type!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.940
Flame Swordsman's Deck Master ability!

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:46.940
He gives 700 attack points!

00:17:53.480 --> 00:17:56.080
3200 attack points?

00:17:56.080 --> 00:17:58.920
He's now stronger than Berserk Dragon!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.150
That's all I can do for now.

00:18:01.150 --> 00:18:03.370
Yugi, I leave the rest to you!

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:04.150
Yeah.

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:06.590
I end my turn!

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:08.840
Thank you, Jonouchi.

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:11.900
I couldn't win this duel without you.

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:14.280
What's the meaning of this, Ooka?

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.930
You said Jonouchi would hinder Yugi!

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:20.020
But he's helping Yugi perfectly!

00:18:20.520 --> 00:18:22.710
This wasn't supposed to happen.

00:18:23.170 --> 00:18:25.450
It's my last turn!  I draw!

00:18:25.930 --> 00:18:27.060
Here I go!

00:18:27.060 --> 00:18:32.890
Dark Magician Knight attacks Berserk Dragon!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.610
Berserk Dragon is destroyed!

00:18:55.760 --> 00:19:00.050
The Big Five, your Deck Masters are destroyed!

00:19:00.050 --> 00:19:03.850
So we win this duel!

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:06.850
We lost...

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:10.360
Hooray!  They won!

00:19:10.360 --> 00:19:12.500
You did great, brother!

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:15.960
Honda, you can get your body back.

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:18.630
Thanks, Yugi!  Thanks, Jonouchi!

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:27.540
As promised, give Honda's body back.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:32.380
Our only option is to take your bodies by force!

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.960
You're dirty!

00:19:47.600 --> 00:19:49.530
What happened?

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:51.560
How disgusting, The Big Five.

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:52.800
Noa!

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:55.430
I no longer need you.

00:20:00.600 --> 00:20:02.210
They're gone.

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:05.680
How horrible.  Just when we won our duel.

00:20:05.680 --> 00:20:11.860
No way...  I'll never be human again!

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:15.320
I'll be a monkey forever?

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:22.530
Poor Honda.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:25.530
Maybe this isn't so bad.

00:20:29.660 --> 00:20:30.670
Noa!

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:33.670
Losers are pathetic.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.260
Right, Mokuba?

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:38.660
Losers don't deserve to exist.

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:42.440
We don't have Honda's body!

00:20:42.440 --> 00:20:44.020
No!  Since when?

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:49.260
Noa, please give us one more chance.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.960
We want actual bodies!

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:55.130
Please, Noa!

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:57.740
Please give us another chance!

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:07.240
You really believed that you'd get bodies if you won your duels?

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.680
Say what?

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:18.200
There is nothing real in this virtual world.

00:21:20.040 --> 00:21:23.680
You tricked us!

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:31.320
You were too dumb to realize it.

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:49.360
We defeated The Big Five, but we're still stuck in the virutal world.

00:21:49.360 --> 00:21:52.840
We need to settle this with Noa face-to-face!

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:56.560
What?  Kaiba is already battling Noa!

00:21:56.560 --> 00:22:00.520
Noa's secret is revealed in this world of creation.

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:03.760
What's the relationship between Noa and Kaiba?

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:07.840
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Noa vs Seto
The Duel at Creation

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.320
Duel, standby!

00:22:13.720 --> 00:22:21.620
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:21.620 --> 00:22:30.570
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:35.540
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:35.540 --> 00:22:39.510
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:39.940 --> 00:22:47.480
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:47.480 --> 00:22:51.050
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:55.820
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:55.820 --> 00:23:05.930
And walk it without stopping

00:23:05.930 --> 00:23:13.540
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:22.510
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:22.510 --> 00:23:30.490
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:30.490 --> 00:23:40.330
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
